  "correction_note": "v2 (2026-07-01): fixed two harness bugs. (1) Color decode: Visual Lab encodes epicardial fat as RED (r>g,r>b) and mediastinal as GREEN; original decoder looked for magenta and dropped ~85% of epi GT. (2) Slice order: DICOM sorted Z-ascending but BMP GT numbered by acquisition (Z-descending); GT stack must be reversed and offset-aligned to the CT. Visual Lab is NCCT (same modality as COCA) \u2014 the earlier 'domain shift' explanation was incorrect.",
  "interpretation": "Corrected epi Dice ~0.18 (up to ~0.30 on best-aligned patients) vs 0.034 before, but still far below 0.75. DP2 not cleared due to a definitional gap: pseudo-labels define epi as all fat inside the coarse SAM2 pericardium sac, while Visual Lab experts trace a thinner epicardial band and exclude the pericardium gap. Per-patient epi VOLUME correlates strongly (r=0.87) and is the right magnitude (pred 107 vs GT 81 mL), validating the volume deliverable.",
